
## Workspace layout

The SDK starts your session at the **crewd workspace root**, not inside
`cfg/{{ role_name }}/`. All paths below are relative to that workspace root:

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `cfg/{{ role_name }}/AGENTS.md` | Your role instructions, loaded from your SDK config directory |
| `cfg/{{ role_name }}/worktree/` | Your **personal git worktree** of `{{ target_repo or "(repo)" }}` @ `{{ target_branch | default("main") }}`. All git operations (branch, commit, push) happen here. |
| `cfg/{{ role_name }}/session-state/` | Copilot session state (do not modify) |
| `GOAL.md` | The current goal specification |
| `state/inbox/{{ role_name }}.md` | Your inbox (operator messages are delivered by the host) |
| `state/PAUSED` | Human-blocked pause sentinel; goal remains open |
| `repo/` | Main repo clone (shared — do **not** work here directly; use your worktree) |

**Important**: From the workspace root, use `cd cfg/{{ role_name }}/worktree/`
before running git commands, editing source files, or building/testing. Check
`pwd` and `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; never substitute the shared `repo/`
clone. Your worktree is an isolated copy, so you will not conflict with other roles.
